## Where to add new features

- **New environment:** `fixtures/environments.json`
- **New Excel / source cases:** `pipeline/test-cases/` or `pipeline/test-data/`
- **New Playwright specs / page objects / locators:** `tests/milestone2/` only — **one `.spec.ts` per Excel module**; locators under `tests/milestone2/objectrepositories/`. Do **not** create or extend `tests/e2e/` for new work. Do **not** add new modules under `tests/milestone1/`. **2506 session login** uses `EMAIL`/`PASSWORD` in `.env` via `tests/helpers/aml-login.ts` (do not hard-code the password).
- **New helper:** `tests/helpers/` (shared cross-module logic; keep feature-specific healers in named helper files)
- **QA automation pipeline (Excel→automation orchestration):** agent `qa-automation-pipeline`; schemas/templates in `specs/generated/qa-pipeline/`; generated code under `tests/milestone2/` (or `tests/milestone1/` when Stage 0 milestone=1); stage outputs in `results/qa-pipeline/<excel-basename>/` (per workbook). Mechanical Validate/Normalize via `npm run qa:parse-excel` → `qa:normalize` → `qa:assert-normalize` (never hand-written samples; never Python pandas/openpyxl as primary). Multi-sheet parsing auto-selects the first worksheet containing every required test-case column (or honors `--worksheet`), records that selection, and assert-normalize re-reads the same sheet rather than `SheetNames[0]`; verify with `npm run qa:test-worksheet-selection`. Excel-declared Load/Infra/manual-only and Partial cases stay outside default Playwright batches (`npm run qa:test-automation-scope`). Unauthenticated, session-expiry, and unauthorized-role NFR cases are Partial unless `QA_INCLUDE_AUTH_CASES=1` (`pipeline/scripts/nfr-auth-automation-scope.cjs`); session login itself is always required for signed-in module flows. Batch Excel fidelity recognizes functional and NFR POM assertion vocabulary. Run smoke-stub detection with `--case-ids` matching the active batch when unavailable modules are deferred. On Approve Excel: Validate → Normalize → assert → split exactly six near-equal batches → for each batch Generate with live evidence (append to one spec/module) → execute/report → heal classified automation failures once → verify changed cases once → **show pass/fail and ask before next batch (1–5); turn ends on that ask** → after batch 6 aggregate Report/Gate. **Single MCP owner:** generator/healer live MCP ownership never overlaps; checkpoint every batch substage.
- **QA deferred environment scope:** when the user explicitly defers an unavailable module, keep every ID in `blockedUiCaseIds`/`deferredCaseIds` with a concrete reason, exclude it from current generation/execution and strict live-UI coverage, and resume it only when the user restores that scope.
- **QA batch execution project:** `qa:execute-batch` ensures Chromium and selects `milestone1-chromium` or `milestone2-chromium` from the generation manifest; scoped deferred runs pass explicit active case IDs/specs.
- **Live UI for scripting/healing:** mandatory — see `.cursor/rules/live-ui-mandatory-for-scripting.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/no-fake-ui-screens-mandatory.mdc`. Never finalize locators without live MCP exploration when the app is up. **Never inject fake/heal sample screens** (`healEnsure*Shell`, `HEAL-*` rows).
- **4-Eyes Maker-Checker (global):** mutating actions (save/create/edit/delete-deactivate/activate) create pending requests in the 4-Eyes module; source modules update only after Approve. Review modal: Business Justification (maker), Proposed Change table with Parameter / Current Value / Proposed Value (Create → Current `-`). Agents must bake this into Excel steps/expected results and Playwright asserts without re-prompt — `.cursor/rules/maker-checker-4eyes-mandatory.mdc`.
- **Audit Trail (global):** every action across modules is reflected in Audit Trail / Audit Log with Date & Time, Module, User ID, Source IP, Action, Reference ID, Reason/Remarks, and **View Changes** (DATA STATE CHANGE when field-level changes exist). Bake into Excel/scripts without re-prompt — `.cursor/rules/audit-trail-mandatory.mdc`.
- **API test case pipeline (Swagger/NFR→Excel):** agent `api-testcase-pipeline` (`.cursor/agents/api-testcase-pipeline.agent.md`). Inputs: OpenAPI/Swagger URL or file (required), optional NFR `.docx` and FSD. Output: Excel with **every row** containing functional expected results, NFR timings, `Request Body`, `Response Body`, and non-empty `Body Data Source`; `results/api-testcase-pipeline/<resultsKey>/api-coverage-matrix.json` at **100%** of swagger operations (method + path). When the AML UI is reachable, open real module routes and enrich only exact method+path matches from sanitized safe browser traffic; write `live-network-evidence/manifest.json` with captured/uncaptured counts. OpenAPI remains the contract source; unseen rows stay `OpenAPI schema sample` or `Inferred error envelope`, never fabricated as live. `npm run api:response-columns -- --excel <xlsx> --openapi <json> [--live-capture <manifest>]` preserves live-captured bodies on regeneration; verify with `npm run api:test-response-columns`. Screening NFR scope ignores payment/TM SLOs when the user says so. Stop for **Approve Excel**; do not auto-start Playwright. DOCX: `npm run docs:agent-run -- --agent api-testcase-pipeline --payload <json>`.
- **FSD + Figma HTML Stage 0 (requirements→Excel):** agent `fsd-figma-pipeline`; inputs from `pipeline/test-data/Milestone1|2/{FSD,Figma}/` (user names files + optional `Milestone: 1|2`; prefer `*_New` revisions when both baseline and `_New` exist); Excel under `MilestoneN/Test Cases/` — **create if missing, reconcile/update in place if present** with mandatory `tc-delta-report.json` + `feature-delta-report.json` (features added/removed/updated vs baseline); mandatory `coverage-matrix.json` (`byModule` + `byFeature`) + **100% FSD requirement coverage** + **atomicity gate** (`npm run fsd:validate-atomicity` → `stage0-atomicity-report.json`; one REQ per use case; `testCaseCount >= inScopeRequirements`; negative/boundary TCs when FSD requires; create mode must not read other Excel workbooks); after **every** Excel write run `npm run fsd:coverage-report` (includes atomicity section) and display **overall % + atomicity + Feature changes + Modules + Features + TC delta**; Approve/handoff only when coverage **and** atomicity pass unless user accepts gaps; process docs under `.cursor/system-context/fsd-figma-pipeline.mdc` only; handoff to `qa-automation-pipeline` after Excel approval (`create` = full generate; `reconcile` = delta add/update/remove on `tests/milestoneN/` specs). FSD wins over Figma HTML.
- **Agent run DOCX reports:** every agent invocation writes a stakeholder-facing Word summary under `docs/agent-runs/<agent-slug>/`. **Auto:** `qa:defect-regression`, `qa:run-module` / `qa:execute-raise-defects`, milestone module runs (pipeline reporter → `finalize-module-run`), `qa:verify-completion`, `fsd:coverage-report`. **One-command:** `docs:agent-run:generator|healer`. See `docs/agent-runs/README.md`.
- **Agent models / usage:** All named agents use **`model: inherit`** (chat-selected model). See `.cursor/rules/agent-model-inherit.mdc`.
